[decoded] "During the day, sunlight travels through the atmosphere, scattering shorter wavelengths of blue light more effectively than longer ones. This phenomenon, known as Rayleigh scattering, causes the sky to appear blue. As the sun sets, the light path through the atmosphere becomes longer, allowing longer wavelengths like red and orange to travel further. Eventually, these colors mix with the blue sky, creating a vibrant sunset. This is why the sky appears blue in the morning and red at sunset."
